In article <1993Jan30.114441.3801@pollux.lu.se>, magnus@thep.lu.se (Magnus
Olsson) writes:
[...]
 > I just downloaded and tested this, and it seems _really cool_. 
 > 
 > I've got one complaint, though: it's so slow that it's virtually
 > unplayable. I tested it on a PS/2 model 70: 80386DX processor, 4 M of
 > RAM, no TSR's loaded, RAMDISK option set to the correct path (and the
 > ramdisk is about 2M large), DOS 3.3 (it's not my machine, and the
 > owner doesn't care about upgrading). 
 > 
 > On this machine, every move took maybe a quarter of a second. That may
 > not sound like too much, but when running through a shortish corridor
 > takes 15 seconds you get a bit impatient. As a contrast, 3.0j runs
 > much faster on a 12 MHz 286 without any ramdisk. 
 > 
 > So, am I doing something wrong, is there somethign wrong with the
 > hardware or setup, or does one really need a workstation to play this
 > game? 

You don't need a workstation, but a better os.  I use a 386 with 8Mb
running os/2.  (No ramdisk) There is no disk activity at all except when I go 
from one level to another.  It is at least as fast as 3.0, and a lot more fun. :-)
  
If you have to use msdos, get a dos 5.0 diskette and load dos into high memory.
That should give about 630kB free.  You may also try a version compiled with
DJGPP.  It use a dos extender wich allows the game to use all the 4MB.  You
should disable the ramdisk in this case.


